---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout
  title="Smart TV Control - URemote — a local TV remote for iPhone and iPad"
  description="A local TV remote for iPhone and iPad. Control an LG webOS, Samsung Tizen, or Android/Google TV over Wi-Fi — find the TV, type in the 6-digit pairing code, share setups by QR, and set up shortcuts. Requires iOS 26 or later."
  applicationSchema
>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <p class="eyebrow load-rise" style="--i: 0">For iPhone &amp; iPad</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title" class="load-rise" style="--i: 1">Your TV remote.<br /><span>On iPhone and iPad.</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-copy load-rise" style="--i: 2">Control a compatible LG, Samsung, or Android/Google TV over your own Wi-Fi. Find the TV, enter the code it shows you, and take control. No account, no cloud, nothing in between.</p>
      <div class="hero-links load-rise" style="--i: 3">
        <a class="button" href="#features">Take a look <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        <a href="#compatibility">Will it work with my TV?</a>
      </div>
      <p class="availability load-rise" style="--i: 4">TestFlight available per request.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-screen load-rise" style="--i: 2">
      <img src={`${base}images/remote.png`} width="1320" height="2868" alt="TV controls with a directional pad, volume, playback, and assigned shortcuts." fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
      <figcaption>Everyday controls, together.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="features" class="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Setup, pairing, sharing, shortcuts</p>
      <h2 id="features-title">Set up. Pair. Share. Make it yours.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <article class="feature">
        <div class="feature-copy">
          <span class="feature-number" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
          <h3>Find your TV.</h3>
          <p>Join your TV&rsquo;s local network, allow Local Network access, and pick your TV from the list. Approve the first pairing on the TV itself.</p>
        </div>
        <figure>
          <img src={`${base}images/setup.png`} width="1320" height="2868" alt="The Add a TV screen with options to find nearby TVs or scan a QR code." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>Find a TV on your network.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>
      <article class="feature">
        <div class="feature-copy">
          <span class="feature-number" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
          <h3>Type in the code.</h3>
          <p>Some TVs pair with a six-digit code instead of a prompt. Your TV shows the code; you type it into six boxes that fill as you go. Wrong code? The boxes shake, clear, and you try again.</p>
        </div>
        <figure>
          <img src={`${base}images/pairing.png`} width="1206" height="2622" alt="The pairing screen with six rounded boxes for entering the 6-digit code shown on the TV." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>Six boxes, one code.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>
      <article class="feature">
        <div class="feature-copy">
          <span class="feature-number" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
          <h3>Pass the remote.</h3>
          <p>Share a saved setup by QR with someone you trust. They scan it or import the image &mdash; &ldquo;Point the camera at a QR code shared with you.&rdquo; The TV may still ask for approval.</p>
        </div>
        <figure>
          <img src={`${base}images/sharing.png`} width="1320" height="2868" alt="The Scan QR Code screen with camera and saved-image import options." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>A shared setup, without an account.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>
      <article class="feature">
        <div class="feature-copy">
          <span class="feature-number" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
          <h3>Your usual buttons.</h3>
          <p>Six shortcut slots for each TV. Assign apps, controls, or volume presets where your TV supports them, with your own names and haptics.</p>
        </div>
        <figure>
          <img src={`${base}images/customize.png`} width="1320" height="2868" alt="The shortcut editor with choices for a TV&rsquo;s shortcut slots." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>Choose apps, controls, or volume presets.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="screenshot-note">Simulator screenshots with sample TVs.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="compatibility" class="details-section" aria-labelledby="compatibility-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Before you begin</p>
      <h2 id="compatibility-title">Local by design.</h2>
      <p>Smart TV Control - URemote talks directly to your TV. No account, cloud relay, or home server is needed.</p>
      <figure class="library-screen">
        <img src={`${base}images/library.png`} width="1320" height="2868" alt="The TV library showing several sample TV cards and an Add a TV option." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>A place for each TV.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <dl class="requirements">
      <div><dt>Your device</dt><dd>iPhone with iOS 26 or later, or iPad with iPadOS 26 or later.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Your TV</dt><dd>LG webOS, Samsung Tizen, or Android/Google TV. Compatibility and available controls vary by model and firmware; not every TV has been verified.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Your network</dt><dd>Your device and TV must be on the same local network. Your device uses Wi-Fi; the TV can use Wi-Fi or Ethernet. Allow Local Network access and approve initial pairing on the TV.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <aside class="privacy-note" aria-labelledby="sharing-title">
    <h2 id="sharing-title">Share a QR like you would share a key.</h2>
    <p>A setup QR can contain reusable TV authorization. It is not encrypted. Anyone with a copy may control that TV from its network, so share only with trusted people. Deleting a saved remote does not revoke a shared copy.</p>
    <a href={`${base}privacy/`}>How the app handles your data <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </aside>

  <section class="closing" aria-labelledby="help-title">
    <h2 id="help-title">Need a hand?</h2>
    <p>Start with the basics: your network, TV approval, and device permissions.</p>
    <a href={`${base}support/`}>Setup help &amp; support <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </section>
</Layout>
